    "body": "### Problem\n\nTyping past shown Insert mode completion candidates with multicursor present on the same line produces strange results when 'completeopt' option contains `noselect` and one of `menu` / `menuone` to show completion list.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean`\n2. `:set completeopt=menu,noselect`\n3. Type `i` - `aa` - `<CR>` - `bb cc dd` - `<Esc>` to add a necessary text.\n4. Type `^` - `Q` - `ww` to add one multicursor and position main cursor on `dd`.\n5. Type `ciw` - `<C-n>` (shows completion candidates) - `aa`. This will hide completion list (because candidates are exhausted) and increase indent. Typing couple of another `a` also results in unexpected text edits.\n\nHere is a demo:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0bb00edb-cacb-4539-8fd3-0e2c53746b8f\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nUsing Insert mode completion with any value of 'completeopt' should not have effect on text edits that cascade during multicursor.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1531+g48864161cd\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, doesn't have this functionality\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.1.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage and from source",
